# pcbdrill: an imaginary PCB drilling machine, 700 x 600 mm, on a cast
# iron base, retrofitted with stmbl. A short, stiff gantry on two Baldor
# LMCF12F; the heavy high-speed spindle with its pressure foot rides on an
# LMCF12E. Point-to-point at 2 g: what counts is how fast each hole's
# position settles. Numbers are made up.
#@dynwiz 20000 20000 1200
drive y1 pcbdrill_y.conf ../sim.txt 60.96
drive y2 pcbdrill_y.conf ../sim.txt 60.96
drive x pcbdrill_x.conf ../sim.txt 60.96
origin 350 300
stroke -5 605 -5 705
frame 1800 500 20 18 22 0.06
rails 0.85
bridge 28 1.7
carriage 6 0.03
racking 6e5 0.02
head 9 0.04 70 85 52 0.03
guidey 20 25
guidex 12 15
# the supply's 2200 uF and the drives' 3 x 470 uF, and a brake chopper: at
# 2 g the drives' own capacitors alone tripped on overvoltage
bus 3610 230 0.5 360 22
home 350 300
